# The national unit for china: a person from the country's past who changed how people live. Items
# take n=4. Dates are in engine/notation/chronicle.ts with their sources.
lesson history-g2-china-a-life-that-changed-things v=1 format=teach grade=2 unit=9 subject=history nation=china levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Yuan Longping"
  goal "Tell the story of Yuan Longping in order, and say what changed for people because of it."

  look {
    scene 36x9 {
      row all at=canvas(1, 0) space=2 align=end {
        person p pose=stand age=grownup hair=short colour=brown top=mint
        timeline line from=1700 to=2000 step=50 years=[] labels=[]
      }
    }
    say """
      Yuan Longping was born in 1930. In 1961 he found a wild rice plant in a field that gave him an idea. In the 1970s he grew the first hybrid rice, which gives much more grain from the same field, so that many more people could have enough to eat.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked history.person-what n=4 k=0
      show history.person-which-first n=4 k=0
      show history.person-order n=4 k=0
      show history.person-line n=4 k=0
      show history.person-changed n=4 k=0
      show history.person-what n=4 k=1
      show history.person-which-first n=4 k=1
      show history.person-order n=4 k=1
    }
    level medium {
      show history.person-what n=4 k=0
      show history.person-order n=4 k=1
      show history.person-line n=4 k=0
      show history.person-changed n=4 k=1
      show history.person-which-first n=4 k=1
      show history.person-order n=4 k=2
      show history.person-line n=4 k=1
    }
    level hard {
      show history.person-what n=4 k=1
      show history.person-which-first n=4 k=1
      show history.person-order n=4 k=2
      show history.person-line n=4 k=2
      show history.person-changed n=4 k=1
      show history.person-order n=4 k=1
      show history.person-line n=4 k=1
    }
  }
  story {
    level easy {
      show history.person-changed n=4 k=1
    }
    level medium {
      show history.person-changed n=4 k=0
    }
    level hard {
      show history.person-changed n=4 k=0
      show history.person-line n=4 k=0
    }
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show history.person-why n=4
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show history.person-retell n=4
  }
  remember {
    say "Yuan Longping changed how people live. We remember a person for what changed because of them."
  }

  grown-ups """
    The idea is that one person's life can change how everyone lives, and that we judge a person
    from the past by what changed because of them rather than by how famous they were. The way in
    names what Yuan Longping did; the core puts the events of the life in order, counts the years between
    them, and says what was different before and after; the two-star question asks for a reason to
    remember them. The wrong idea to watch for is "important because famous". If the child is
    stuck on the years, count on to the next ten first. The three-star task is for you to mark:
    the story in three sentences, in order, with a year. Off the page, find a picture of Yuan Longping
    together and ask what the child would want to ask them. China's 道德与法治 in the first grades asks children to learn about people who have served the country, and Yuan Longping is one most families know.
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level a worked example names what Yuan Longping did, the years are counted from the birth, and the events come nearly in order; the core ends with the before-and-after question in both forms."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the events are muddled both ways, the years are counted both from the birth and between the later events, and the first question compares the life with an event from another lesson only a few years apart."
  }
}
